@startuml
title ExitPass POS Server Counters and Recovery Continuity Model

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

rectangle "Fiscal state" #F3FFF3 {
    component "Sales Invoice\nsequence" as SISeq
    component "Adjustment document\nsequence" as AdjSeq
    component "Reset counter" as Reset
    component "Z-counter" as ZCounter
    component "Grand Total Amount\naccumulator" as GTA
    component "Latest EJ hash" as EJHash
    component "Last fiscal event\ntimestamp" as LastEvent
}

database "Backup / restore /\nfailover input" as Backup
component "Continuity check" as Check
component "Supervised recovery\ngate" as Gate
database "Recovery audit\nrecord" as Audit
component "Fiscal issuance\nresume / block" as Resume

SISeq --> Check
AdjSeq --> Check
Reset --> Check
ZCounter --> Check
GTA --> Check
EJHash --> Check
LastEvent --> Check
Backup --> Check

Check --> Resume : continuity proven
Check --> Gate : continuity not proven
Gate --> Audit : approval, reason,\nreference notes
Audit --> Resume : controlled resume\nor continued block

note bottom of Check
POS Server must never resume from lower counters,
lower Grand Total Amount, earlier SI sequence,
or broken fiscal continuity.
end note

note bottom of Reset
Reset counter increments only on fiscal reset.
Z-counter advances per Z-reading / fiscal day close.
end note

@enduml
